WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.530
Sell safely, keep records, and find your best-sellers.

2
00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:07.850
This is the video for module four of Handmade Accessories for Sale.

3
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:14.340
You do not need every channel. You need the one or two places your buyer already spends time.

4
00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:20.570
You need a fixed way to handle every order, so nothing is lost and no one cheats you.

5
00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:26.080
Your own taste is a poor guide to what sells. Your records are a good one.

6
00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:30.940
And at the end, you plan your next 90 days from that evidence.

7
00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:43.660
Set up WhatsApp Business, separate from your personal WhatsApp, with a catalogue of your products, quick replies and labels like Paid and Sent. When someone asks, send the catalogue link.

8
00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:50.800
Confirm the item, total price, delivery fee, payment method and delivery day in one message.

9
00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:56.580
Check the payment in your own bank or wallet app before anything leaves your hands.

10
00:00:57.830 --> 00:01:03.140
Pack carefully, and add a small thank-you card with your WhatsApp number and care instructions.

11
00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:07.460
A few days later, follow up and ask how it is going.

12
00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:14.020
Watch for these tricks. Fake payment alerts are common, so always check in your own app.

13
00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:21.880
Some buyers overpay and ask you to refund the difference. Never refund until the full amount has cleared.

14
00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:32.370
And ignore messages offering paid verification or promotion of your page. Never share one-time passwords or PINs with anyone.

15
00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:44.480
Ada displays earrings by colour and builds matching sets of earrings, bracelet and headband at a set price. She checks every transfer in her app before handing over goods.

16
00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:50.000
She sells 14 pairs of earrings at 2,500 naira.

17
00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:53.190
9 bracelets at 2,000.

18
00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:56.380
And 3 sets at 8,000.

19
00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:12.410
That is 77,000 naira in sales. But sales are not profit. After the table fee, transport and the cost of the pieces, she knows her real profit. She also collects 11 phone numbers for new stock updates.

20
00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:22.240
Write one line per sale on the day: date, product, quantity, price, cost, channel and customer's first name. Keep a stock count too.

21
00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:30.960
Each month, work out profit per product: price minus cost, times the number sold. That shows what really earns money.

22
00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:42.280
Then sell-through: pieces sold, divided by pieces made, times 100. 80 percent means it is in demand. 20 percent means it is sitting.

23
00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:48.900
And count repeat customers. Repeat buying is the strongest sign your quality is right.

24
00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:59.010
For example, Funmi's earrings sold 26 out of 30, that is 87 percent. Her totes sold 6 out of 8. Both are make more.

25
00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:10.450
Her statement bracelets sold well, but earned only 200 naira each because they take 50 minutes. So she raises the price or simplifies the design.

26
00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:21.170
Her headbands sold only 3 out of 10. Before making more, she asks buyers why. Is it quality, price, or fit? Each needs a different fix.

27
00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:29.830
Now plan. Days 1 to 30, focus: make more of your best-sellers and fix one costing or quality problem.

28
00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:39.530
Days 31 to 60, grow: add one channel, such as a boutique on consignment, or one tested new design. Not both.

29
00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:49.630
Days 61 to 90, review: compare your numbers with your starting month, and drop what is not working. Give every step a number and a date.

30
00:03:50.880 --> 00:04:03.470
To remember. Sell where your buyer already shops. Confirm every payment in your own app. Log every sale on the day. Let profit and sell-through decide what to make. And plan with dates and numbers.

31
00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:17.090
Now open your first channel, start your sales log, and assemble your capstone with your reflection and 90-day plan. Small, honest sales with clear records are worth more than a big story.

32
00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:19.380
Continue with the lessons below.
